{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuntrgT7vyV76Tcim7om","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"As far as I know, Cloudflare Workflows has **no built-in per-workflow concurrency setting** in `wrangler.toml`/`wrangler.jsonc`. The only cap is the platform's account-level limit on concurrently running instances, and you can't lower it for one workflow. Check the current Workflows \"Limits\" docs in case a setting has been added since.\n\nTo cap concurrency yourself, the usual pattern is a **Durable Object acting as a semaphore**:\n\n- Make the first `step.do()` in the workflow ask the DO for a slot.\n- If no slot is free, wait and retry with `step.sleep()`. Alternatively, have the DO record the instance ID and later wake it with `instance.sendEvent()` while the workflow waits on `step.waitForEvent()`.\n- Release the slot in a final step, and also on failure, for example with try/finally around your steps.\n\nA simpler option is to throttle **creation** instead. Route requests through a Cloudflare Queue and have the consumer call `env.MY_WORKFLOW.create()` only when the number of running instances (tracked in a DO or KV) is below your limit. Queue `max_concurrency` on its own won't work, because `create()` returns as soon as the instance starts, not when it finishes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d9cfabd-b48f-4d79-a7db-f32103e9e133","uuid":"769ad917-0c74-4c9a-b35d-130249fbc232","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:08:18.510Z","request_id":"req_011CfuntrSK6RQ9igy4sfUno"}
